From eafffd77596a4efcdfea58c71c9f8c1a4cdb374e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:19:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: join two Dolby Vision tracks of Matroska that
 libavformat does not group, once their packets show them

libavformat groups two Matroska HEVC tracks only by a profile 7 record with the enhancement layer on
one of them. Files in use are also made without any record (mkvmerge before v81 did not read Dolby
Vision from a transport stream), or with the record that mkvmerge writes for the RPU of a MEL
(profile 8, no enhancement layer). Such a pair played as HDR10.

Where libavformat makes no Dolby Vision group and the file has exactly two HEVC tracks, one of the
size of an enhancement layer of the other, both framed with lengths, and no record that speaks
against it, Find() reports the pair unverified. Its base packets wait, no longer than for a missing
layer, until the first packets say it: the second track brings the RPU of a dual-layer stream and no
units of type 63, the first track none. Then the base stream becomes Dolby Vision profile 7
(VideoPlayer opens its codec again and chooses its output as for a new file). Otherwise the pair is
refused before any packet goes out: what waited goes out as it was read, then every packet as it is
read, two streams as before.
